export anchor HotelConciergeStyle:
    number: 87
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Hotel concierge
    idea: The dashboard arrives as a grand hotel's letter on cream stationery under an embossed crest, with every project hanging as a brass room-key fob in a pigeonhole rack and each fact put politely.
    base: light
    palette:
        lobby: #ebe7df, the page around the sheet
        stationery: #fdfbf6, the letter sheet
        navy: #1d2b47, text, rules, progress bars and the primary button
        slate: #55607a, notes, times and the last week line
        linenLine: #d8d2c4, hairlines, never text
        brass: #b4914d, the crest, room plates and the focus glow, never text
        brassInk: #6d5520, eyebrows and the desk bell
        fobBrass: #e7d5a6, the key fobs
        pine: #2f6045, On track
        amber: #8a5300, At risk
        burgundy: #7a1f2f, Behind and the overdue notice
    type:
        Two stacks. Garamond, EB Garamond, Baskerville, Palatino Linotype,
        Georgia, serif for everything you read, with the greeting at 44px
        italic, room numbers 40px, the brand 30px caps tracked 0.42em,
        folio numbers 30px, section titles 28px and body 18px with 1.55
        line height. Gill Sans, Optima, Segoe UI, sans-serif at 600 for
        10 to 13px caps tracked 0.2em on eyebrows, nav, floors and buttons.
    layout:
        A cream sheet up to 1140px with a navy top edge floats on a taupe
        lobby. The letterhead is centred, an embossed crest with a shield,
        a B and laurels, the spaced caps brand and an italic motto. A desk
        row between two hairlines holds an underlined search asking How may
        we help, the New project button, a desk bell and the guest name.
        The nav is one centred caps line with brass dots between items. The
        letter has a right aligned date, an italic Good morning, Mara, a
        short polite paragraph and a burgundy notice with a clock saying 4
        tasks are overdue, signed by the desk. Beside it a framed guest
        folio lists the four numbers with dotted leaders. The key rack is a
        three column grid of pigeonholes ruled in navy, each with a brass
        room plate, a hook and a brass fob rounded at the top with the
        room number 101 to 106, the floor named after the team, the
        project, tasks with a thin bar, the departure date and the status.
        Below, Messages for you shows six message slips with the sender
        and time in a side column, and a housekeeping report shows a
        dashed line for last week and a solid line for this week. Below
        960px panels stack and the rack goes two across, then one.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 56px sheet margins, 40px between letter parts and 20px inside pigeonholes.
    density: Low to medium. A letter, a folio of four lines and six fobs.
    corners: Square paper and rack. Key fobs are rounded 120px at the top and 28px at the foot.
    borders: 1px navy rules with a 4px inset linen line on the folio. Thin brass plates on each pigeonhole.
    shadows: The sheet floats on a soft 32px shadow and fobs hang with a 6px shadow. The crest has a one pixel light and dark emboss.
    icons:
        Fine 1.5px line icons and a desk bell for notifications. On track
        is a filled diamond, At risk a filled triangle, Behind a filled
        circle with a bar and overdue a clock, each in a small enamel chip
        with the caps word.
    focus: A 2px navy outline offset 3px with a 6px brass glow. A focused field gets a 2px underline and a warm fill.
    tone: Courteous and formal, such as Kindly note, We would suggest, With our compliments and Departure 14 Nov.
